(a) No retail package dealer of distilled spirits shall operate such business in connection with any other mercantile establishment, except licensed packaged beer and wine. A package dealer may not sell or display or keep in stock for retail sale any other products or services, except for the following inventory:
(1) Beverages containing no alcohol and commonly used to dilute distilled spirits may be dispensed through the use of vending machines, but no beverages of any kind may be opened or consumed in said place of business; and
(2) Packaged ice (in packages of five (5) pounds or greater), ice chests, and "koozies" (individual can and bottle coolers);
(3) Cigarettes, cigars, chewing tobacco, alternative nicotine products, or vapor products, snuff, if properly licensed to do so, cigarette papers, lighters and matches, chewing gum, breath mints, packaged consumable single-serving snack items not requiring any preparation for consumption, single-serving pain medications, and over-the-counter birth control devices;
(4) Paper, styrofoam, or plastic cups, gift bags, which are limited in size to accommodate one (1), seven hundred fifty (750) ml. size bottle of wine or distilled spirits, and contain only products approved for sale or display by this regulation;
(5) Lottery tickets issued by the Georgia Lottery Corporation and any approved Georgia Lottery Corporation lottery materials, provided such retailer is also an authorized retailer of the Georgia Lottery Corporation;
(6) Bar supplies, limited to corkscrews, openers, straws, swizzle stirrers, and bar-related containers, cocktail olives, onions, cherries, lemons, limes, and sugars or salts produced and marketed specifically for the preparation of alcoholic beverage drinks, alcoholic beverage drink recipe booklets, bar guides, and consumer-oriented alcoholic beverage publications.
(7) Products co-packaged with alcoholic beverages, provided that the products are limited to items approved for sale or display by this regulation, are offered for sale and sold as a single unit, and do not include more than one (1) type of alcoholic beverage product;
(8) Check cashing services arising out of the sale of any product lawfully sold under this rule;
(9) Money order sales arising out of check cashing services;
(10) Automated teller machine service for customer use; and
(11) Gift certificates for use only at the issuing licensed retailer.
(12) Notwithstanding any other provisions of this paragraph, any legal business may adjoin or abut either or both a package liquor store and package beer and wine store, provided all building requirements in this section are met; and provided further that there shall be no doorways whatsoever located between any adjoining businesses other than between businesses neither of which is licensed to sell beer, wine, or distilled spirits; except a door is authorized between adjoining package liquor and package beer and wine stores which must be closed and locked during days and hours when the operation of either place of business is prohibited.
(13) Coin-operated devices, similar machines on premises. It shall be unlawful for a retail dealer in spirituous liquors by the package to permit any gambling on the premises by use of coin-operated devices and it shall be unlawful for any person to play or operate for the purpose of gambling, pinball machines, machines for amusement purposes, coin-operated machines for dispensing tobacco products or packaged ice and the violation of this section shall be punishable as provided in section 9-3 of the city Code.
(14) Each licensee shall conspicuously display within the interior of the licensed premises a printed price list of the alcoholic beverages offered for sale or, in lieu thereof, shall place the price of each item on the container or on the shelf were the container is exhibited for sale.
(15) No retailer of packaged distilled spirits shall sell such beverages at a price less than the cost which such licensee pays for such distilled spirits.
(Ord. No. 810, § 1, 2-11-19)

